---
kind: lore
id: east.ashgrove
title: Ashgrove, the lantern town
---

// Ashgrove: Ash Tower, the monster graves, Elder Rook's house. The first
// visit is east.ashgroveArrival; the tower is scenes/east/ash-tower*.lute.

// ── services ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<beat id="center" on="heal" target="town.ashgrove" title="Monster Center" once="false">
  ::use{component="nurse" town="ashgrove"}
</beat>

<beat id="mart" on="shop" target="town.ashgrove" title="Mart" once="false">
  ::use{component="shop" stock="ashgroveStock"}
</beat>

// ── walking in, after the first visit ───────────────────────────────────

<entry id="eastAshgroveMorning" on="enterTown" target="town.ashgrove" category="ambient" priority="5" once="day" when="@isMorning">
  @narrator: Morning mist sits in Ashgrove's streets like it pays rent. The tower bells are silent.
</entry>

<entry id="eastAshgroveDay" on="enterTown" target="town.ashgrove" category="ambient" priority="5" once="day" when="run.slot == 'day'">
  @narrator: Ashgrove is quiet at midday too. Someone is sweeping the steps of the tower, very slowly, as if the steps might mind.
</entry>

<entry id="eastAshgroveNight" on="enterTown" target="town.ashgrove" category="ambient" priority="5" once="day" when="@isNight && clock.weekday != 4">
  @narrator: At night the paper lanterns along the eaves glow by themselves. Nobody in Ashgrove will tell you who lights them.
</entry>

<entry id="eastAshgroveFridayNight" on="enterTown" target="town.ashgrove" category="ambient" priority="8" once="day" when="@isNight && clock.weekday == 4">
  @narrator: Friday night. The whole town is walking up the hill to the tower, lanterns held high, not saying a word.
</entry>

// ── Yun the lantern-maker: eastLanterns ──────────────────────────────────

<beat id="yunLanterns" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveLanternMaker" title="A lantern for the tower" priority="10">
  @ashgroveLanternMaker: You're the one who came through the tunnel. Can you carry a lantern? Not now. On a Friday night.
  @ashgroveLanternMaker: Every Friday we walk our lanterns up the tower for the monsters we've lost. This year we've a stranger's hands and fewer of ours.
  @ashgroveLanternMaker: Or, if you'd rather: bring me a ghost. A friendly one. They carry the light better than any of us.
  ::accept{quest="eastLanterns"}
</beat>

<entry id="eastYunBark" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveLanternMaker" category="bark">
  @ashgroveLanternMaker: Paper, wire, a little oil, and somebody to remember. That's all a lantern is.
</entry>

<entry id="eastYunMorning" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveLanternMaker" category="bark" priority="5" when="@isMorning">
  @ashgroveLanternMaker: I make lanterns in the morning and sell them at night. The morning ones are better. I'm less tired.
</entry>

<entry id="eastYunDone" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveLanternMaker" category="bark" priority="20" when="quest.eastLanterns.state == 'complete'">
  @ashgroveLanternMaker: Your lantern's on the fourth floor, by the window. I checked. It's still lit.
</entry>

// ── Caretaker Bea ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

<entry id="eastBeaWorried" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveCaretaker" category="bark" when="run.lair.towerSiege != 'cleared'">
  @ashgroveCaretaker: I look after the monsters whose trainers have passed on. There's room for more, I'm sorry to say. And now no Elder Rook to help.
</entry>

<entry id="eastBeaRelieved" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveCaretaker" category="bark" when="run.lair.towerSiege == 'cleared'">
  @ashgroveCaretaker: Rook's home, grumbling about his knees. That's how I know he's fine. Thank you. The whole house thanks you.
</entry>

// ── Hobb the gravekeeper ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

<entry id="eastHobbBark" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveGravekeeper" category="bark">
  @ashgroveGravekeeper: Every name on that tower wall, I've carved. Two thousand and eleven. Mostly spelled right.
</entry>

<entry id="eastHobbNight" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveGravekeeper" category="bark" priority="10" when="@isNight">
  @ashgroveGravekeeper: Night's when they visit. Don't look so pale. I mean the families. Mostly the families.
</entry>

// ── Nell and her puffsong ────────────────────────────────────────────────

<entry id="eastNellBark" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveMourner" category="bark" when="run.lair.towerSiege != 'cleared'">
  @ashgroveMourner: My puffsong used to sing me to sleep. Now I can't even reach her candle.
</entry>

<entry id="eastNellAfter" on="talk" target="npc.ashgroveMourner" category="bark" when="run.lair.towerSiege == 'cleared'">
  @ashgroveMourner: I lit her candle again. I sang to it this time. It's only fair.
</entry>

// ── Elder Rook, home again ───────────────────────────────────────────────

<entry id="eastRookHome" on="talk" target="npc.elderRook" category="bark" when="run.lair.towerSiege == 'cleared'">
  @elderRook: The flute is for the great sleeper on the Silvercrest road. It will not like being woken. Nobody does. Be ready.
</entry>

<entry id="eastRookMorning" on="talk" target="npc.elderRook" category="bark" priority="5" when="run.lair.towerSiege == 'cleared' && @isMorning">
  @elderRook{emotion="happy"}: Tea? No? Young people. Three days tied to a chair and all I wanted was tea.
</entry>

<entry id="eastRookFlute" on="talk" target="npc.elderRook" category="bark" priority="10" when="run.lair.towerSiege == 'cleared' && holds(caught(slumbear))">
  @elderRook{emotion="happy"}: You woke it, and it came with you. Then it was waiting for you, all those years. I am glad I kept the flute.
</entry>

// ── Ash Tower's ground floor, on later visits ─────────────────────────────

<entry id="eastTowerHallBesieged" on="enterPlace" target="place.ashTowerHall" category="ambient" priority="5" once="day" when="run.lair.towerSiege != 'cleared'">
  @narrator: The candles in the hall are burning low. Nobody has dared go up to light new ones.
</entry>

<entry id="eastTowerHallFree" on="enterPlace" target="place.ashTowerHall" category="ambient" priority="5" once="day" when="run.lair.towerSiege == 'cleared'">
  @narrator: Fresh candles on every ledge, all the way up the stairs. On the third step, someone has left a single sprig of heather.
</entry>
